<linker>
  <!--
    The runtime assembly is preserved whole because very little of it is reachable by
    static analysis:

      * AirshipUtils.Serialize and Deserialize reflect over the public fields and
        properties of every config and model type.
      * Deserialize builds JsonArray<T> through MakeGenericType and invokes FromJson by
        name, so those instantiations only exist at runtime.
      * EnumExtensions.ToStringValue and ParseEnumFromStringValue read enum fields and
        their [AirshipEnumStringValue] attributes reflectively.
      * The ten Airship.AirshipListener callbacks are invoked by name from the native
        layers through UnitySendMessage, never from managed code.

    Managed stripping above Minimal removes these, and every resulting failure is silent:
    a config payload missing fields, an ExecutionEngineException on a generic array, or
    events that simply stop arriving. Preserving the assembly is cheap, since it is small,
    and the alternative is a member list that goes stale with every new model.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="AirshipSDK" preserve="all"/>
</linker>
